## Purpose
- Give fast operational commands for local bring-up and smoke checks.

## Source of truth
- `docker-compose.yml`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/package.json`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Properties/launchSettings.json`
- `services/team-hub-gateway/team-hub-gateway/Properties/launchSettings.json`

## Do
- Full stack via docker:
  - `docker compose up --build`
- Expected host ports after start:
  - gateway `https://localhost:7172`
  - auth (direct) `http://localhost:5112`
  - postgres `localhost:5433`
- Frontend local (from `frontend/team-hub-web`):
  - `npm install`
  - `npm start` (uses proxy to gateway)
- Quick auth smoke through gateway:
  - `POST https://localhost:7172/api/auth/register`
  - `POST https://localhost:7172/api/auth/login`
  - `POST https://localhost:7172/api/auth/refresh` (with cookie)
  - `POST https://localhost:7172/api/auth/logout`

## Don't
- Do not run heavy builds/tests for docs-only updates.
- Do not verify auth flow by bypassing gateway when checking end-to-end.

## Checklist
- Containers healthy (`postgres`, `auth`, `gateway`).
- Gateway route `/api/auth/*` reaches auth service.
- Frontend can authenticate with cookie-based refresh flow.
